{"id": "EUVD-2026-108857", "enisaUuid": "f6c9f5c0-c385-3f77-8df2-ef1448273fef", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nksmbd: fix lease break and ack state handling\n\nDo not skip valid lease states containing WRITE_CACHING when breaking\nlevel-II/read leases for writes and truncates.\n\nHandle lease break acknowledgments according to the SMB2 rule that the\nacknowledged state must be a subset of the server's break target. Apply\nthe acknowledged state directly and keep the break pending on failed ACKs.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:31:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:31:37", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/17699905a381621c1cee5b6528feb05acedc86a4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3251ea36df5eef58aa207fbee48849d89b922ea6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fba4653a0b4dc2f6d42600abe21fb326292f70ff", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5015191096db311759fef98769270336cd8b1324", "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-98901"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98901", "GHSA-6w2x-j37m-r6r9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "06cfd88d-5942-3d2b-ba3d-5bebdf00dc90", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "52b64582-2df8-3675-8c16-f11a14952c52", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "61af3603-e783-32bd-90de-865c00526ff2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <17699905a381621c1cee5b6528feb05acedc86a4"}, {"id": "75b35618-df48-3112-ac52-e3a58d9a4352", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <5015191096db311759fef98769270336cd8b1324"}, {"id": "7c06824d-e9b5-3586-b740-62b9efda0255", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c